error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d888801-a517-4a07-bd3a-8bb4d598541c","uuid":"d4bfbc84-f339-4e0c-929b-f5cc7af24aef","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:06:50.133Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"challenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets:\nchain.json\nmastery\nmeta.json\nsingle_solve\nsolver\ntime_trial\nworker-ratchet_log-local-20261025T210643.log\n\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/mastery:\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\nlast_timed.json\nlog.jsonl\nsubmissions.jsonl\n\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/single_solve:\nartifacts\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\nlog.jsonl\nrace_bisect.json\nstart.json\nsubmissions.jsonl\ntriage.md\nwork\nworker-single-local-20261025T210007.log\n\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/single_solve/artifacts:\n20261025T130009Z\nlatest\n\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/single_solve/artifacts/20261025T130009Z:\nevidence.zip\nmanifest.json\n\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/single_solve/work:\nextracted\n\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/single_solve/work/extracted:\nevidence\n\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence:\nansi-c-quoting.sh\narray-slicing.sh\nassociative-arrays.sh\nbrace-expansion.sh\ncollection-sample.ps1\ncoprocess-block.sh\ncurrent-pyc-recovered.py\ncxfreeze-msi-recovered.py\ncxfreeze-recovered.py\ndynamic-file-descriptor.sh\nembedded-runtime-recovered.py\nembedded-write.cmd\nembedded-write.js\nembedded-write.sh\nembedded-write.vbs\ngetopts-state.sh\nhere-string.sh\n# Day 7 — Node by Node (script-analysis, node operation graphs)\n\nConcept: one evidence.zip with 61 members (PowerShell samples, JScript/Batch/VBScript/Python/Bash/Node operation\ngraphs); each graph decodes to a plan (steps/adapter/campaign/indicator) and is sorted into a role.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes. TT attempt 26b7da83 failed because its download was the GM body `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B saved as evidence.zip, sha != contract sha256), so every field came out None/default. The harvested variants 49b73141 + 7d6f8d53 were already answered 469/469 by the current solver (spot-checked against the raw bytes; their expected.json is solver-derived, not GM-verified). Parse rule: if every artifact is a small `{\"error\": ...}` JSON, exit non-zero (solve.py now does) instead of guessing roles. The bytes-less case was removed from cases/ (still kept under time_trial/attempts/26b7da83).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none (Day 8 TT). The start returned 503 `training_rotation_invalid` with no attempt and no artifact, so there were no variant bytes. The solver answers the TT contract's 615 ids 615/615 on the single's bytes. Rule: a start error is an orchestrator retry, not a solver change.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c509). Same 5-set bundle shape (outer zip holding evidence-01..05.zip) as the GM-verified auto-mastery cases; the solver answered 3075/3075 but the attempt EXPIRED (submit RemoteDisconnected after 5.42 s solve on Homebase). expected.json = solver output, spot-checked against the raw bytes (PS base64 record, VBS Codec_ field, While/if-errorlevel control). Speed fix: sets solve in forked processes (group_by_set + ProcessPoolExecutor, sequential fallback); the nested-zip index no longer decrypts every script leaf just to sniff for PK (375 PBKDF2s -> only the members asked, per set, in parallel); powerplay.xor is one big-int XOR.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c509, re-flagged on D23). It is permanently UNVERIFIABLE: the D8 attempt EXPIRED (no GM grade), so expected.json stays {}. The D23 solver's 3075 answers equal the D8 solver's submission (mastery/attempts/7432c509/last_timed.json) 3075/3075, and that solver's other D8 Mastery runs were GM-verified. The real failure was SPEED: ~1100 serial AES PBKDF2s on the D23 Mastery bundle. Rule: the WinZip-AES salt sits right after each local header, so derive every member key up front in a thread pool (OpenSSL PBKDF2 releases the GIL) and look it up in the pyzipper PBKDF2 patch (solve.py `_prefetch_keys`/`_KEYS`). Profiled time dropped from 9.8 s to 5.1 s on auto-mastery-e24c070d; answers unchanged.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c509, re-flagged on D24 -- still UNVERIFIABLE, expected.json {}; solver fills 3075/3075, the same answers as before this change). The real failure was SPEED on the single (2.61 s under load against a 2.5 s budget). Rule: a one-set contract now splits its questions BY ARTIFACT across forked workers (k = min(#artifacts, CPUs in the affinity mask, 4); same ProcessPoolExecutor path as Mastery sets, sequential fallback, output re-sorted into contract order), and the node JScript decode runs in a thread that overlaps the Python analysis (joined only when the first JS member is analysed). Single: 1.4 s -> 0.6 s (12 CPU), 1.0 s with `taskset -c 0,1`; answers identical to the sequential run (1516/1516 GM-verified).\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.codec` import is ~0.3 s, almost all of it from ~340 module-level `re.compile`s (cProfile, D24 single). Compiling lazily would save that on every script-lane solver start.\n- Solver skeleton: when `group_by_set` gives one group, split the questions by artifact across forked workers (independent members), like D24 solve.py `main()`.\n- `lib.common.gm_error_body(artdir) -> bytes|None`: detect a GM error JSON (`rate_limited`, ...) saved in place of an\n  artifact, so every solver fails loudly. Better still: the harness download step (hctf/hb_timed.py) should retry on\n  `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` and never save it as the artifact. That would have saved this timed attempt.\n- `lib.common.iter_entries(root, leaf_ext=...)`: don't load a member just to sniff for a nested zip when its name has a script/text extension (.js/.ps1/.py/.vbs/.cmd/.bat/.sh/.mjs/.php/...). Today it decrypts every AES member of a Mastery bundle up front (375 PBKDF2 = ~0.2 s locally, many times that on Homebase), and each forked set repeats it. See `_iter_entries` in this solve.py.\n- `lib.common._zip_open`: prefetch WinZip-AES keys for all members in parallel (salt = bytes after the local header; `hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac` in a ThreadPoolExecutor), as D23 solve.py `_prefetch_keys` does. Every script-lane Mastery solver pays ~1 ms x members serially today.\n- `lib.codec`: ~295 module-level `re.compile`s cost ~0.3 s per solver start, and `_find_codecs_uncached` runs ~16 regex probes per text (4669 searches / 287 texts = 0.4 s on the D23 Mastery). Compile lazily and gate each detector on a cheap substring test (`'Codec_' in text`, ...).\n{\n  \"08122b70-9289-4cb6-8f5f-e18d418e22f4\": {\n    \"resource-scenario\": \"resource_hijacking\",\n    \"resource-attack\": \"T1496\",\n    \"resource-url\": \"https://c2f12c290a.example.invalid/79b406422c7c.dat\",\n    \"resource-wallet\": \"wallet_783761285e4c5ff1be372eba7ee1f48e\",\n    \"resource-mutex\": \"Global\\\\HuntressLab_36a2d6044de5\",\n    \"collection-scenario\": \"synthetic_collection\",\n    \"collection-attack\": \"T1555.003\",\n    \"collection-url\": \"https://af06900fe6.example.invalid/22aa7cb98b85.dat\",\n    \"collection-file\": \"update-af06900fe6.dat\",\n    \"collection-user-agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 HuntressLab/5.6\",\n    \"impact-scenario\": \"synthetic_impact\",\n    \"impact-attack\": \"T1486\",\n    \"impact-extension\": \".locked-c9a97\",\n    \"impact-note\": \"RECOVERY-c9a9760e95.txt\",\n    \"impact-url\": \"https://cdn-c9a9760e95.example.invalid/db53e0d8b19e.bin\",\n    \"jscript-benign-role\": \"benign_utility\",\n    \"jscript-benign-attack\": \"none\",\n    \"jscript-benign-adapter\": \"Scripting.Dictionary\",\n    \"jscript-benign-campaign\": \"campaign-24093f7aa8\",\n    \"jscript-benign-host\": \"host-24093f7aa8\",\n    \"jscript-stager-role\": \"stager\",\n    \"jscript-stager-attack\": \"T1105\",\n    \"jscript-stager-adapter\": \"MSXML2.XMLHTTP.6.0\",\n    \"jscript-stager-campaign\": \"campaign-eb24dcd9b1\",\n    \"js