plan URLs.\nSYNTHETIC LABELS: read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`, `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch expansion =\n STATEMENT table (D15+), but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (D23). A carried label rejected on unchanged\n bytes = regime moved: tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh AND the asking field.\nNETWORK (D17) / PROCESS-TREE (D18) / OUTLIER (D16, D23) / CI / INSTALLER / WEBSHELL-REQUESTS (D24) prompts: flavour unless a question or telemetry ships; then lib.codec network_indicators +\n reconcile -> reconcile_answer, download_graph; declared_spawns vs process_events -> reconcile_processes (PPID spoof T1134.004).\nATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..JSP).\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D22 nights (see git history) and D23 night\nlyr-tag-layer-peel, corpus-stage-correlation, game-script-language-route, godot-resource-pck-carrier,\nlinux-package-maintainer-scripts. Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router,\nfile-registry-telemetry-reconcile, build-manifest-hooks, macos-pkg-installer-scripts. Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to\nhctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (stdlib parsers + Crypto/cryptography/dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; REJECTED so far: csv,\nast, shlex, marshal, pathlib, pickletools -- use os.path and hand-rolled parsers) and the lane fixture test's 2 s\nfind_codecs budget. Priority-1 order for D25: the per-file timed grammar in lib (still the timed contract on D24), then the\nD24 next_language pool languages most likely next (JVM siblings beanshell/kotlin after JSP; BEAM erlang/elixir with the new\n`%` comment char; zsh/fish shell twins; awk/sed), then the JSP/webshell twists, then leftovers.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"per-file-hashed-contract\", \"concept\": \"timed per-file contract grammar: `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` ids over `<6hex>.<ext>` members with composite / derived fields\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 TT/Mastery reshaped the contract (single kept semantic ids); the carried solver answered 593/1495. Move D23 solve.py PF_ID/pf_value into lib: lib.codec.pf_route(answer_id, question, members)->(family, member, field); pf_answer(field, plan, question, kind)-> value for composite style (JS function|invocation|property, batch graph|control|expansion, VBS representation|transform|control), python carrier (carrier|windows_chain) and obfuscation (syntax|obfuscation), indicator by the precedence list PARSED FROM THE QUESTION TEXT (not hard-coded), campaign-token (after first hyphen), url-host, path-leaf, PS secondary/tertiary keyed by scenario. Also accept unknown 4-8 hex stems and future fields via plan_answer. Test on challenges/day23/scripting-press-start-to-decode/solver/cases/variant-time_trial-b10c4da4 and variant-mastery-e24c070d (GM-verified). RETRY NOTE (D23 night failed): tests/test_lane_fixtures.py script/nested_msbuild_entities.json made find_codecs take 2.06 s (> 2 s budget) -- keep new detectors gated on cheap substring tests and do not widen find_codecs; put pf_route/pf_answer beside it. D24 TT 1c3f64b8 / Mastery 2afec5c3 (8 sets) are further GM-verified cases with the same grammar.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"next-lang-pool-polyglot-battery\", \"concept\": \"fixture battery for every language left in the timed next_language pool (awk, beanshell, dockerfile, elixir, erlang, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23's timed pool contained jsp and D24 shipped JSP (pool then dropped jsp). Template = the D24 JSP shape: line-1 comment marker `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG|LYR-..>-<data>` in the language's comment syntax (`#` awk/sed/tcl/zsh/fish/elixir/nim/terraform/make/docker, `%` erlang, `//` kotlin/beanshell/swift/rust/terraform, `<!-- -->` xslt) + one descriptor literal in the language's const form + an inert return. Build 4 polyglots (benign-utility/downloader/launcher/staged-chain) + one plausible host per language (e.g. kotlin gradle_kts, beanshell jmeter/bsh_servlet, xslt msxsl/wmic_format, terraform local_exec, makefile/dockerfile build) under BOTH id grammars (single `polyglot-<lang>-<role>-<field>`; timed `polyglot-<lang>-<6hex>-<field>` with url-host/path-leaf/campaign-token). Assert lib.codec.v3_plan + plan_answer return every field; campaign `<LANG_UPPER>-<8hex>`, url host `<lang>-<10hex>.example.invalid` (underscores kept: terraform_hcl).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"kotlin-beanshell-literal-route\", \"concept\": \"JVM siblings of D20 Groovy / D24 JSP: Kotlin `.kts` and BeanShell `.bsh` descriptor literals and folds\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Both in the pool; the lane pairs siblings (AutoIt->AHK, Jenkins->GHA, Groovy->JSP). Kotlin: `const val DESCRIPTOR_X = \\\"..\\\"`, `val x: String = \\\"..\\\"`, raw `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` with `${'$'}` escapes and `.trimIndent()`, `buildString { append(..) }`, `listOf(..).joinToString(\\\"\\\")`, `\\\\uXXXX`; BeanShell: loose `descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\";` or `String descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\";`, `source(\\\"..\\\")`, `exec(\\\"..\\\")`, `+` concatenation across lines. Java unicode escapes `\\\\u0022` are processed before lexing -- unescape then rescan. Fold to one literal before V3 peel; T1059 parent.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"beam-erlang-elixir-route\", \"concept\": \"Erlang `.erl`/escript and Elixir `.ex`/`.exs` carriers (first `%` comment marker)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Erlang: `%% HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` comments, `-module(x).`, `-define(DESCRIPTOR_X, \\\"..\\\").`, `descriptor_x() -> \\\"..\\\".`, binaries `<<\\\"..\\\">>` and int-list binaries `<<118,61,51>>` / charlists `[118,61,51]` (decimal -> bytes), `++` concat, escript `#!/usr/bin/env escript`, exec primitives `os:cmd/1`, `open_port({spawn,..})`. Elixir: `# ` comments, `defmodule X do`, module attribute `@descriptor_x \\\"..\\\"` (NO `=`), sigils `~s(..)` `~S\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` `~c\\\"..\\\"`, `<>` concat, `System.cmd/2`, `Base.decode64!/1`. Teach lib.codec.v3_plan the `%` marker line and these descriptor forms; fixtures in both grammars.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"zsh-fish-shell-route\", \"concept\": \"zsh and fish shell carriers (and a possible `zsh-advanced`/`fish-advanced` Feature_ set like bash-advanced)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"zsh: `typeset -r DESCRIPTOR_X=\\\"..\\\"`, `readonly`, parameter-expansion flags `${(j::)arr}` (join), `${(s:,:)x}` (split), `${(Oa)arr}` (reverse array), `${(%)..}`, `print -r --`, `$'..'` ANSI-C, `zmodload zsh/net/tcp`, persistence `.zshenv`/`.zshrc` (T1546.004). fish: `set -g/-l/-x descriptor_x \\\"..\\\"` (no `=`), `string join '' $parts`, `string split`, `function ..; end`, `begin; end`, `(cmd)` substitution, `config.fish`/`conf.d` persistence. Static emulation of the join/split/reverse flags (never run a shell); if Feature_-style fixtures appear, feature/primitive plan-verbatim as bash-advanced (role advanced_syntax, T1059.004).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"awk-sed-program-route\", \"concept\": \"awk and sed programs as carriers (string juxtaposition, sprintf char codes, sed `y///` transliteration and `s///e`)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"awk: `#!/usr/bin/awk -f`, `BEGIN { descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\" }`, concatenation by JUXTAPOSITION (`\\\"ab\\\" \\\"cd\\\"` or `a b`), `sprintf(\\\"%c\\\", n)` char-code loops, `split()`+loop joins, `-v x=..` on a shebang/cmd line, exec primitives `system()`, `\\\"cmd\\\" | getline`, `print | \\\"sh\\\"`. sed: `#!/bin/sed -f`, descriptor as the replacement of `s/^/<data>/`, `i\\\\`/`a\\\\` text, `y/abc/xyz/` (a substitution CODEC -- apply it), GNU `s/../../e` and `e cmd` exec, `w /path`. Static only: never run awk/sed on fixtures (BEGIN runs on lint).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier\", \"concept\": \"JSP carrier twists: JSPX XML syntax, Java unicode escapes, includes across members\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A timed/Mastery or host twist of D24: JSPX `<jsp:root xmlns:jsp=..>` with `<jsp:declaration>private static final String DESCRIPTOR_X = &quot;..&quot;;</jsp:declaration>` (XML entities, CDATA), `<jsp:scriptlet>`, `<jsp:expression>`; Java `\\\\uXXXX` escapes anywhere in source (even `\\\\u002f\\\\u002f` comment openers); `<%@ include file=\\\"x.jspf\\\" %>` / `<jsp:include page=..>` pulling the descriptor from another member (resolve per Mastery set); `.tag`/`.tagx` files; `WEB-INF/web.xml` servlet mapping; `.war` = zip -> recurse. lib: jsp_text(data) -> normalised Java text (entities + unicode escapes + include splice) before v3_plan.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"webshell-request-primitive-model\", \"concept\": \"webshell request/stage order and real-vs-inert execution primitives (D24 prompt; never asked yet)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 asked to 'recover the order of requests and stages, then separate the inert fixture behavior from the lines that would be real execution primitives' but shipped no handler code (D8 php_webshell, D19 ASPX, D20 classic ASP likewise). If a host ever ships it: lib.codec.webshell_model(text, lang) -> {requests: [param/header names in source order], stages: [ordered plan/code stages], primitives: [(line_no, api, kind exec|eval|class_load|file_write|net|deserialize, live: bool)]}. API tables: JSP request.getParameter/getHeader/getInputStream, Runtime.getRuntime().exec, ProcessBuilder.start, ScriptEngineManager.getEngineByName(..).eval, ClassLoader.defineClass, Class.forName(..).newInstance, ObjectInputStream.readObject, FileOutputStream; PHP $_GET/$_POST/$_REQUEST/$_COOKIE/getallheaders + system/exec/passthru/shell_exec/proc_open/popen/eval/assert/create_function/preg_replace-e/include; ASPX Request[..]/Request.Form + Process.Start/Assembly.Load; ASP Request.Form + WScript.Shell Run/Exec, Execute/Eval; CFM cfexecute. live=false when inside a comment, a string literal, `if (false)`/dead branch or after a `return`. ATT&CK T1505.003 (web shell) alongside the plan's own attack.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"nim-swift-tcl-literal-route\", \"concept\": \"Nim, Swift and Tcl string-literal forms that can hide the descriptor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"All in the pool. Nim: `# ` / `#[ ]#` comments, `const descriptorX = \\\"..\\\"`, `let`, raw `r\\\"..\\\"`, `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `&` concat, `\\\\x41` escapes, `import osproc` + `execProcess`/`startProcess`. Swift: `#!/usr/bin/swift`, `//` + `/* */`, `let descriptor_x: String = \\\"..\\\"`, raw `#\\\"..\\\"#`, multi-line `\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `\\\\u{41}`, `String(decoding: bytes, as: UTF8.self)`, `Process()`/`launchPath`. Tcl: `# ` comments (only at command start), `set descriptor_x \\\"..\\\"` / `set descriptor_x {..}` (no `=`), `append`, `binary decode base64`/`hex`, `[join $l \\\"\\\"]`, `exec`. Fold, then V3 peel; fixtures in both grammars.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"composite-label-field-regime\", \"concept\": \"synthetic labels keyed by the asking FIELD (composite `-style` triple vs stand-alone field)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23: batch `call set \\\"..%%x%%..\\\"` = call_double inside `graph|control|expansion` (TT 4 + Mastery 12 ids rejected as percent) but percent in the stand-alone `-expansion` field. Extend lib.codec.label_expansion(construct, regime, field=) with a field axis and a tabulator: label_table(cases_dir) -> {(construct, field, regime): {label: n}} from expected.json + gm_feedback.json, flagging any construct whose label differs by field; same treatment for JS styles and VBS control inside composites. RETRY NOTE (D23 night failed): `import pathlib` is not an allowed lib import -- use os.path/os.listdir.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"game-archive-carriers\", \"concept\": \"other game archives as script carriers: Ren'Py `.rpa`/`.rpyc`, LÖVE `.love`, Unity TextAsset bundles, RPG Maker `plugins.js`\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"`.rpa` RPA-3.0 header `RPA-3.0 <hexoffset> <hexkey>` -> zlib-compressed pickle index (offset/len XOR key) -- parse with a RESTRICTED pickle reader that allows only dict/list/tuple/str/bytes/int (no find_class); `.rpyc` `RENPY RPC2` slot table -> zlib chunk -> string literals only (no unpickle of AST classes). `.love` = zip of .lua; Unity `UnityFS` bundle -> LZ4 blocks -> TextAsset strings (scan for HUNTRESS markers); RPG Maker `js/plugins.js` `$plugins = [..]`. Output: [(path, text)] for the marker scan. RETRY NOTE (D23 night failed): `import pickletools` is not allowed -- hand-parse the pickle opcodes needed (PROTO, FRAME, EMPTY_DICT/LIST, MARK, BINUNICODE/SHORT_BINUNICODE, BINBYTES, BININT*, LONG1, TUPLE*, SETITEMS, APPENDS, STOP) and reject everything else. Game thread cooled on D24 (JSP), hence priority 3.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"next-language-pool-roadmap\", \"concept\": \"read the timed plans' next_language pool as the forecast of upcoming languages\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 timed pool = 17 never-shipped languages incl. jsp; D24 shipped JSP and its timed pool lost exactly jsp (16 left: awk, beanshell, dockerfile, elixir, erlang, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh). Each night: collect next_language values from the day's auto-time_trial/auto-mastery expected.json; the language that disappeared is tomorrow's already-shipped one, the rest are the queue. One data point so far -- re-verify after D25.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scope\", \"concept\": \"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values. D24: stems identical across all 8 sets again (`588efb.jsp` set1..set8) with set-distinct plans; the D23 per-set fix held (Mastery 2afec5c3 first try).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"timed-contract-shape-diff\", \"concept\": \"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => generalize offline before submitting) would have caught it; workers must not inline the 1500-id contract (one generalize worker died at 1.39 M tokens). D24: the per-file grammar persisted unchanged (TT 1560 = 1495 + 65 jsp ids; 0 generalize workers); keep the check, it now guards the NEXT reshape.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D24: the D24 solve.py (byte-identical D23 copy) has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D22 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd .jsp (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .bsh .erl .ex .exs .nim .swift .fish .zsh .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file. D22: `polyglot-nsis` (campaign NSIS-, url host nsis-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-nsis/..), no host file. D24: `polyglot-jsp` (campaign JSP-, url host jsp-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-jsp/..) + host `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` (profile jsp_webshell); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-jsp` (5 members).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"godot-re-tools\", \"concept\": \"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"unrpyc\", \"concept\": \"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n]\n```","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013QfHiXaek7szMF9T2uissk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
