blings) |\")\nrep(\"Counts: 99 rows; seen 36 (rows 1-18, 22, 30 (GHA only), 35, 48-52, 67, 70, 75, 77 (JSP D24; Java/Kotlin gap), 82 (NSIS D22), 89-91 + 94\\n(D23)), gap 63 (rows 95-99 opened by D24;\",\n\"Counts: 99 rows; seen 37 (rows 1-18, 22, 30 (GHA only), 35, 48-52, 67, 70, 75, 77 (JSP D24; Java/Kotlin gap), 82 (NSIS D22), 89-91 + 94\\n(D23), 95 (Elixir D25; Erlang gap)), gap 62 (rows 96-99 opened by D24;\")\nfor r in ('| 25 |','| 32 |'):\n    old=[l for l in s.split('\\n') if l.startswith(r)][0]\n    s=s.replace(old, old.replace(\"in the D24 next_language pool\",\"in the D24+D25 next_language pool\"))\n# cues (in place, no new lines)\nrep(\"<%-- marker --%> + <%! private static final String DESCRIPTOR_ -> JSP (D24, host jsp_webshell)  -module/-define/`%` -> erlang\",\n\"<%-- marker --%> + <%! private static final String DESCRIPTOR_ -> JSP (D24)  `#` + descriptor_x = / %{..} / defmodule -> elixir (D25, host\\n elixir_phoenix)  -module/-define/`%` -> erlang\")\nrep(\" Still the grammar D24 (TT 1560, Mastery 8 sets). NEXT LANGUAGE = the one that leaves the timed plans' next_language pool.\",\n\" Still the grammar D25 (TT 1625, Mastery 9 sets). NEXT LANGUAGE = the one that leaves the timed next_language pool (2/2 hits).\")\nrep(\"NETWORK (D17) / PROCESS-TREE (D18) / OUTLIER (D16, D23) / CI / INSTALLER / WEBSHELL-REQUESTS (D24) prompts: flavour\",\n\"NETWORK (D17) / PROCESS-TREE (D18) / OUTLIER (D16, D23) / CI / INSTALLER / WEBSHELL (D24) / CONFIG-DRIFT (D25) prompts: flavour\")\nrep(\"v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..JSP).\",\"v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..Elixir).\")\n# readiness gaps\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"); k=s.index(\"```json\",i); e=s.index(\"```\",k+7)\ngaps=json.loads(s[k+7:e])\ndrop={\"per-file-hashed-contract\",\"next-lang-pool-polyglot-battery\",\"kotlin-beanshell-literal-route\"}\ng={x['id']:x for x in gaps if x['id'] not in drop}\nBUDGET=\" RETRY NOTE (D24 night failed): tests/test_lane_fixtures.py `find_codecs` 2 s budget (nested_msbuild_entities 2.18-2.66 s, nested_decoy_random 2.22 s) -- do NOT add detectors to find_codecs; put the new reader beside v3_plan behind a cheap substring gate (or land find-codecs-speed-gate first).\"\nb=g[\"beam-erlang-elixir-route\"]\nb[\"concept\"]=\"Erlang `.erl`/escript carriers (first `%` comment marker) + Elixir twists beyond the D25 shape\"\nb[\"detail\"]=\"Elixir SHIPPED D25 in the simplest form (`# ` marker, `descriptor_<8hex> = \\\"..\\\"`, `%{descriptor: ..}` map, inert Phoenix controller) and the carried solver read it unpatched; Erlang (BEAM sibling) is still in the pool. Erlang: `%% HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` comments, `-module(x).`, `-define(DESCRIPTOR_X, \\\"..\\\").`, `descriptor_x() -> \\\"..\\\".`, binaries `<<\\\"..\\\">>` and int-list binaries `<<118,61,51>>` / charlists `[118,61,51]` (decimal -> bytes), `++` concat, escript `#!/usr/bin/env escript`, `os:cmd/1`, `open_port({spawn,..})`. Elixir timed/host twists: module attribute `@descriptor_x \\\"..\\\"` (NO `=`), sigils `~s(..)` `~S\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` `~c\\\"..\\\"`, `<>` concat, `Base.decode64!/1`, `System.cmd/2`. Teach lib.codec.v3_plan the `%` marker line and these forms; fixtures in both grammars (single `polyglot-erlang-<role>-<field>`, timed `polyglot-erlang-<6hex>-<field>`).\"+BUDGET\nb[\"priority\"]=1\ng[\"zsh-fish-shell-route\"][\"detail\"]+=BUDGET\ng[\"jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier\"][\"detail\"]+=BUDGET.replace(\"D24 night failed\",\"D24 night failed, also killed rc -9\")\ng[\"jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier\"][\"priority\"]=3\ng[\"awk-sed-program-route\"][\"detail\"]+=\" RETRY NOTE (D24 night failed): a `__import__()` call in lib/codec.py was rejected -- use plain top-level imports from hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS only.\"\ng[\"webshell-request-primitive-model\"][\"detail\"]+=\" RETRY NOTE (D24 night): worker killed (rc -9) before writing anything -- scope smaller: tables + one function + 4 fixtures, write the module first, then tests. D25 Phoenix host again shipped no request/exec code (inert `show(_conn, _params)`).\"\ng[\"webshell-request-primitive-model\"][\"priority\"]=3\ng[\"nim-swift-tcl-literal-route\"][\"priority\"]=2\ng[\"awk-sed-program-route\"][\"priority\"]=2\ng[\"zsh-fish-shell-route\"][\"priority\"]=1\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"find-codecs-speed-gate\",\"concept\":\"make lib.codec.find_codecs fast (lazy regex compile + cheap substring gates) so carrier prebuilds stop failing the 2 s fixture budget\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 night: 3 of 6 script-lane prebuilds (beam, zsh-fish, jsp-jspx) failed ONLY on tests/test_lane_fixtures.py find_codecs > 2 s (nested_msbuild_entities.json 2.18-2.66 s, nested_decoy_random.json 2.22 s); D23 night per-file-hashed-contract failed the same way. Profile (solver NOTES D24): ~295-340 module-level re.compile cost ~0.3 s per import and _find_codecs_uncached runs ~16 regex probes per text. Fix inside lib/codec.py WITHOUT changing outputs: compile lazily (functools.lru_cache'd getters), gate each detector on a substring test ('Codec_' / 'CODEC_' / 'HUNTRESS' / 'MATERIAL_' / 'descriptor' case-insensitive) before its regex, short-circuit once a v= plan decodes, and cap per-text work on large decoy members. Acceptance: every existing tests/ fixture returns identical results and both named fixtures run < 1 s. Only stdlib imports from hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (no pathlib/ast/shlex/__import__()).\"},\n {\"id\":\"rust-cargo-buildrs-route\",\"concept\":\"Rust carriers: `.rs` scripts, `build.rs` build-time execution, Cargo manifests\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"rust is in the D25 next_language pool (15 left) and the lane has had no compiled-language source day since C# (D19). Shapes: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` or `//!`/`/* */` doc comments, `const DESCRIPTOR_X: &str = \\\"..\\\";`, `static DESCRIPTOR_X: &'static str`, `let descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\";`, raw strings `r\\\"..\\\"` / `r#\\\"..\\\"#` / `r##\\\"..\\\"##`, byte strings `b\\\"..\\\"` / `br#\\\"..\\\"#`, `\\\\u{41}` and `\\\\x41` escapes, `concat!(\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\")`, `include_str!(\\\"x.txt\\\")` (resolve against a sibling member per Mastery set), `[u8; N]` arrays `&[118, 61, 51]`, `String::from_utf8(vec![..])`. Host candidates: `build.rs` (cargo runs it at build time; T1059 parent / T1195.001 supply chain), `Cargo.toml` `[package] build = \\\"build.rs\\\"`, `[build-dependencies]`. Teach lib.codec.v3_plan the typed `const NAME: &str =` form (type annotation like GDScript D23) and raw-string delimiters; 4 polyglots + a `host-cargo-build-script-rust` fixture in both id grammars. Never run cargo/rustc on fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"terraform-hcl-function-fold\",\"concept\":\"Terraform HCL literal folds: heredocs, interpolation, `join`/`base64decode`/`format` calls\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"terraform_hcl in the pool (family name would be `polyglot-terraform_hcl`, campaign `TERRAFORM_HCL-<8hex>`, url host `terraform_hcl-<10hex>.example.invalid` -- underscores kept like github_actions D21). cloud-iac-userdata-route (built) covers user_data scripts; this gap covers the HCL side: `#`/`//`/`/* */` comments, `locals { descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\" }`, `variable \\\"x\\\" { default = \\\"..\\\" }`, heredocs `<<EOT`/`<<-EOT` (indent strip), `\\\"${local.a}${local.b}\\\"` interpolation over locals, `join(\\\"\\\", [\\\"..\\\", \\\"..\\\"])`, `base64decode(\\\"..\\\")`, `format(\\\"%s%s\\\", ..)`, `replace(..)`, `jsonencode({..})`; hosts `provisioner \\\"local-exec\\\" { command = .. }`, `data \\\"external\\\"` (program = [..]), `null_resource` triggers. Resolve locals/variables statically (no terraform init/plan) before V3 peel; fixtures in both grammars.\"},\n {\"id\":\"stage-config-survival-diff\",\"concept\":\"config that changes shape across a stage chain and the key that 'didn't survive' (D25 prompt; never asked yet)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D25 prompt: 'Configuration starts out in Elixir source and has changed shape by the time an inert Phoenix-hosted stage picks it up. Follow every transformation, reconcile each one with earlier campaign artifacts, and find the setting that didn't survive.' Nothing shipped, but a host day could ship it. lib.codec.config_chain(members) -> ordered [(member, format, {key: value})] parsing Elixir `config :app, Key, k: v` keyword lists / `%{}` maps / `runtime.exs` `System.get_env(\\\"X\\\", \\\"default\\\")`, Erlang `sys.config` terms `[{app, [{k, v}]}].`, `vm.args` `-k v`, `.env` `K=V`, JSON/YAML/TOML, plus every v=3 plan (`k=v|..`); key normalisation (snake/camel/upper, `:atom`, `\\\"str\\\"`); config_diff(chain) -> keys dropped / renamed / value-changed between consecutive stages and vs the corpus plan of the same campaign_id. Answer shapes to expect: the dropped KEY name verbatim, its last value, or the member where it vanished. Stdlib only; hand-rolled term parser (no ast).\"},\n {\"id\":\"eex-heex-template-carrier\",\"concept\":\"Phoenix/Elixir templates as carriers (`.eex`/`.heex`/`.leex`, `~H` sigils, router/endpoint files)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D25's host was a bare controller module; a later host/timed twist could move the descriptor into `lib/<app>_web/templates/*.html.eex` (`<%= @descriptor %>`, `<%# HUNTRESS.. %>` EEx comments), HEEx `~H\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` sigils with `{@x}` attrs, `router.ex` (`get \\\"/stage\\\", InertController, :show` -> request surface), `endpoint.ex` plugs, or `mix.exs` aliases/`compilers:` (build-time execution, like build.rs). Extend the marker scan to EEx comment syntax `<%# .. %>` and HEEx `<%!-- --%>`; read `mix.exs` `aliases:` keyword lists as declared commands. Fixtures for single + timed grammars.\"},\n]\nout=[]\norder=[\"find-codecs-speed-gate\",\"beam-erlang-elixir-route\",\"zsh-fish-shell-route\",\"rust-cargo-buildrs-route\",\"awk-sed-program-route\",\"nim-swift-tcl-literal-route\",\"terraform-hcl-function-fold\",\"stage-config-survival-diff\",\"composite-label-field-regime\",\"jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier\",\"webshell-request-primitive-model\",\"eex-heex-template-carrier\",\"game-archive-carriers\"]\nnd={x['id']:x for x in new}; g.update(nd)\nfor oid in order: out.append(g.pop(oid))\n# notes/tools keep, update the roadmap note\nrm=g[\"next-language-pool-roadmap\"]\nrm[\"detail\"]=\"D23 timed pool = 17 never-shipped languages incl. jsp; D24 shipped JSP and its pool lost exactly jsp; D24 pool had elixir, D25 shipped Elixir and its pool lost exactly elixir (2/2 hits). 15 left for 6 days: awk, beanshell, dockerfile, erlang, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh. Each night: collect next_language values from the day's auto-time_trial/auto-mastery expected.json; the language that disappeared is the day's shipped one. Siblings so far: AutoIt->AHK, Perl->Ruby, Groovy->JSP; the BEAM pair suggests erlang soon.\"\ng[\"mastery-set-scope\"][\"detail\"]+=\" D25: 9 sets, stems again identical across sets (`a7470f.exs` set1..set9); first try.\"\ng[\"timed-contract-shape-diff\"][\"detail\"]+=\" D25: unchanged a 3rd time (TT 1625 = 1560 + 65 elixir ids).\"\ng[\"solver-lib-v3-fallback\"][\"detail\"]=g[\"solver-lib-v3-fallback\"][\"detail\"].replace(\"STILL OPEN after D24: the D24 solve.py (byte-identical D23 copy)\",\"STILL OPEN after D25: the D25 solve.py (byte-identical D23/D24 copy)\")\nlx=g[\"leaf-ext-list\"]; lx[\"detail\"]=lx[\"detail\"].replace(\".gd .jsp (and future\",\".gd .jsp .exs (and future\")\nfn=g[\"family-name-underscore\"]; fn[\"detail\"]+=\" D25: `polyglot-elixir` (campaign ELIXIR-, url host elixir-.., /tmp/huntress-elixir/) + host `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir` (profile elixir_phoenix); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-elixir` (5 members).\"\nout+=list(g.values())\njs=json.dumps(out,indent=None,ensure_ascii=False)\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in out)+\"\\n]\\n\"\npre=s[i:k]\nnewpre=\"\"\"## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D23 nights (see git history) and D24 night\nper-file-hashed-contract, next-lang-pool-polyglot-battery, kotlin-beanshell-literal-route. Given up (2 attempts):\npython-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, build-manifest-hooks,\nmacos-pkg-installer-scripts. Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (stdlib parsers +\nCrypto/cryptography/dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; REJECTED so far: csv, ast, shlex, marshal, pathlib, pickletools,\n`__import__()` calls -- use os.path and hand-rolled parsers) and the lane fixture test's 2 s find_codecs budget (failed 4\nprebuilds -> find-codecs-speed-gate goes FIRST). Priority-1 order for D26: the speed gate, then the pool languages most\nlikely next (Erlang = BEAM sibling of D25 Elixir; zsh/fish shell twins; Rust), then the remaining pool languages (awk/sed,\nnim/swift/tcl, terraform_hcl; kotlin/beanshell, dockerfile/makefile and xslt already have built routes), then the\nnarrative-model gaps (config survival D25, webshell requests D24) and leftovers.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:i]+newpre+\"```json\\n\"+body+s[e:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nF=reference/coverage/script-analysis.md; python3 -c \"\nimport json,re;s=open('$F').read();i=s.index('## Readiness gaps');k=s.index('\\`\\`\\`json',i);e=s.index('\\`\\`\\`',k+7);g=json.loads(s[k+7:e]);print(len(g));\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('script-analysis:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('script-analysis:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(pend),pend); print(set(tuple(sorted(x)) for x in g))\"\nawk '/^## Recognition cues/{f=1} f{n++} /^## Readiness/{print n; exit}' $F; wc -l $F"}}}
